:null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.beta [ef02314], 4.6.stable.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9636) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700H (20 threads) - 15.69 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nDiscovered this bug when triaging https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119645.\n\n- When a scene instance and some of its editable children are selected, \"Move Up/Down\" can edit the order of foreign nodes.\n\nI can open a PR if needed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the MRP, or set it up manually:\n1a. Create a \"main\" scene with several child nodes.\n1b. Create a \"test\" scene with several child nodes.\n1c. Add a scene instance of \"test\" inside \"main\". Make sure that \"test\" is the last child of \"main\".\n1d. Enable \"editable children\" on \"test\".\n2. Hold `Ctrl` to select both \"test\" and the last child of \"test\" inside \"main\".\n3. Make sure the cursor is hovering over the scene tree and not the 2D viewport.\n4. Press `Ctrl + Up Arrow` to move both nodes up the scene tree.\n5. See that both nodes (including the yellow foreign node) are moved up (relative to their siblings) without the \"Alert!\" pop-up.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/22e07560-6a58-4e80-899b-be904e5e40a4\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP_Move_Up_Down_Foreign.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28431883/MRP_Move_Up_Down_Foreign.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url